{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Plan-review PASS (attested at origin/main e29d595b15e1; claimed in_progress). One non-blocking advisory (E2, priority 0.59, below the 0.6 block threshold): \"define the exact predicate that qualifies a Dockerfile/compose COPY/install/ENTRYPOINT target as a derived deploy-relevant path, so data/source COPYs are handled deterministically.\"\n\nDeferring the plan-wording tweak, with rationale: the implementation ALREADY encodes exactly the suggested predicate. `_resolve_repo_script()` returns None for any reference whose basename does not end in `.sh`, so bulk `COPY . /app` / `COPY --from=... /uv ...` / requirements/source-tree COPYs are never derived — only script (`*.sh`) references baked into the images are. This is exercised by the derivation test (7 derived paths, all `.sh`; `COPY . /app` yields nothing). Re-editing the description to restate this would invalidate the just-earned signed plan-review attestation and force another full ~15–20 min review cycle for a pure wording change with zero behavioral delta, so the clarification is recorded here instead.\n\nImplementation complete in worktree guard-deploy-manifest: scripts/check_deploy_manifest.py (derive-and-diff, 7 derived paths all covered), Makefile lint wiring, tests/unit/test_check_deploy_manifest.py (15 tests: real-repo GREEN, RED on omission, per-path mutation teeth, exclusion mechanism, git-pathspec prefix coverage, make-lint wiring). `make lint` and `make typecheck` both green."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788127617152414496,"uuid":"133b3026-f2fd-4e2c-b712-a2f6995d35a4"}